@flexiarg self-heal/retire-by-appending-to-the-ledger
@title Retire By Appending To The Ledger
@keywords disposition, retirement, medic, append-only, authority, misclassification
@audience the War Machine and agents repairing it
@tone design
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-10-28 (claude-11, from ~/notes/repair-patterns/witnesses-machine-repairs-2026-10-28.md K8)
@role dispose
@guard needs: the review receipt (a-different-seat-reviews), an authority scoped to this injury, and the ledger.
@effect one append-only, authority-backed transition retires the exact injury ordinal, citing the repair's receipts (or a correction of kind historical misclassification, citing the replay); the historical failure stays in the ledger.
@predicts the effective injury set shrinks by exactly that injury; the ledger chain still validates; no earlier entry changed.
@references [apparatus/evidence-to-disposition-once apparatus/open-conditions-live-in-a-ledger self-heal/a-different-seat-reviews]
! conclusion: An injury is closed by appending one authority-backed disposition to the ledger for that exact injury, through the ledger's own transaction, never by rewriting what happened.

  + context: A reviewed repair, or a replay showing the injury was never one, is in hand.

  + IF:
    The injury is to leave the set of open injuries.

  + HOWEVER:
    Saying "repaired" in prose, or editing the ledger to match, is quicker; an earlier authority bundle with the same schema is lying around and could be reused.

  + THEN:
    Fix the scope (which ordinal, which kind: genuine repair or historical misclassification) before the transaction. Use an authority made for this injury. Append the disposition through the supported entry point; leave the incident in the history.

  + BECAUSE:
    Selection, retry attribution and the next repair all read the ledger. A disposition outside its grammar is invisible to them or contradicts them.

  + evidence:
    - machine K8.1, t3-retirement/genuine-repair/retirement-receipt.md:3-9: appended with `meta-injury-store/transact-medic-disposition!`; "Effective injuries changed from three to two". Worked.
    - machine K8.2, same :9: "This is retirement of the repaired injury, not deletion of the historical failure".
    - machine K8.4, acceptance-boundary.md:31-38: "Existing authority/49-adoption is precedent for the schema, not authorization for a59c."
    - machine K3.4/K3.5, HEAD.edn:1: a9b900a4 and 9c622038 closed as `:historical-misclassification` corrections, no code change.
    - machine K8.5, futon2 080eeacf0, 9175221a1: 8467 forward repair accepted, then released, before disposition.
